# The input `$81:990B` was ported without, and the one the round that ported it
# said it owed: *"an input that fires a weapon at whatever
# `movies/level29-item.zmv` is walking past 35 times, and the census will name
# `$81:96E4` on the frame it staggers."* It does, 430 times.
#
# **The thing being walked past is the type $1E actor placed at (921,794)** —
# `zamn_assets actors <rom> 29`, entry 6 — and it chases. That is the whole
# trick: `movies/level29-item.zmv` climbs north past it and the creature follows
# a fixed 30 to 80 pixels behind, directly south, in the same column. So this
# movie keeps 3,597 frames of that route unchanged and then turns around. One
# line does it:
#
#     3624   Down+Y
#
# Nothing else is added and nothing before it is touched, which is the only way
# a route survives a change of intent: `tools/fit_route.py`'s note that "firing
# changes what those frames mean" is about legs planned *under* fire, and this
# fires after the last leg has been walked.
#
# **It cannot kill it, and the arithmetic says so before the route does.** From
# `--watch`, the creature's `$2A` starts at `$0097` — 151 — and the squirt gun
# is collision id `$5C`, whose `ENEMY_DAMAGE_TABLE` entry is 1. The player
# starts level 29 with `$7E:1CCC = $0150`, which is 150 rounds in BCD. **One
# short**, before a single shot is allowed to miss.
#
# The player loses first anyway. He arrives on 7 health, the creature takes one
# point every 90 frames while they are touching, and `$7E:1CB8` reaches zero at
# 4262. He respawns on 10 at 4540 and goes back to it; the movie stops at 5150,
# on that second life, with `$2A` at 71 of 151.
#
# What it buys, against the nine sites that had never been reached:
#
#     d990b_hit            315
#     d990b_survived       194
#     d990b_staggered      121
#     d990b_stagger_posted 121
#     react_already         41   — off `enemy_survived_react`, not this family
#
# and the census, which was empty over the whole corpus one round ago:
#
#     handler          $81:96E4          430
#
# **`d990b_stagger_already` is still zero, and the reason is worth keeping.** It
# reads `ACTOR_ATTR_SET` off `$08`'s record — the same bit, at the same offset,
# on the same record that `enemy_survived_react`'s guard reads, and that guard
# fires 41 times here. So the bit is up often enough. It is never up on a hit
# that empties the pool, across 121 of them: the flash is installed by the
# splice a *survivor* posts, and a hit that staggers posts `$81:9643` instead
# and installs nothing. The two guards are not independent, they are exclusive,
# and no amount of the same shooting will cross them.
#
# `movies/level29-990b-freeze.zmv` is the other half: `$5D` on the same
# creature, which is the only other id it answers to that an input can produce.

